# Hermetic E2E Testing — REQUIRED for every implementation

Full standard lives in [`docs/testing.md`](../../docs/testing.md). Read it
before writing tests. Reference: the first hermetic e2e file under
`app/<route>/e2e/` (delivered by Spec 01); until that lands, mirror the
structure of the engine package's
`src/Combat/e2e/combat.engine.test.ts`.

## The rule

Every implementation lands with at least one **hermetic e2e test** that
exercises the change through the highest-level public entry point of
its module. If you cannot write one, extract logic until you can — or
note "hermetic-test debt" with a concrete reason in the PR description.

**Hermetic** = all three of:

1. **Self-contained** — no network, no real `AsyncStorage`, no real
   filesystem, no real font loader, no real `Animated` driver, no real
   timers (use `jest.useFakeTimers()` when timers matter), no real
   image fetching.
2. **Deterministic** — stub `Math.random` (or use the engine's seeded
   `Rng` once available). No wall-clock time, env vars, or PIDs.
3. **Isolated** — `afterEach(() => jest.restoreAllMocks())`; no shared
   mutable state between tests.

**E2E** = drives the change through the public entry point of the
module — the screen's presenter (`select<Screen>ViewModel`) for UI
work; the engine store's lifecycle for state changes — *not* through a
private helper.

## Conventions

- **Location:** `app/<route>/e2e/<feature>.engine.test.ts`. Companion
  engine code at `app/<route>/e2e/<feature>.engine.ts`. Pure unit tests
  stay at `app/<route>/<file>.test.ts`. Component render tests at
  `components/<Component>.test.tsx`.
- **Imports for stubs:** keep `jest.spyOn(Math, 'random')` / fake-timer
  setup in `app/test-utils/` so tests are one-liners. Do not duplicate
  the same setup in every test file.
- **Required suites:** happy path; every state branch the change can
  reach (loading / error / empty / populated for screens, every
  win-condition for combat presenters); invariants (view-model fields
  total — no `undefined` strings, no negative bars); and at least one
  store-lifecycle assertion driving `createGameStore(memoryAdapter, …)`
  through the relevant action and asserting `memoryAdapter.save` was /
  was not called as expected.
- **Screen changes:** the screen `*.tsx` must delegate to a presenter
  function in `*.engine.ts` that has its own hermetic e2e test. Inline
  math / inline data shaping in screens blocks this and must be
  extracted.

## Self-check before declaring done

- [ ] New / updated test under `app/<route>/e2e/` (or
      `components/<Component>.test.tsx` for pure rendering branches).
- [ ] `npm test` green twice in a row (no flakes).
- [ ] All randomness stubbed; no raw `Math.random` in the test.
- [ ] No network, no `AsyncStorage`, no real timers, no real fonts in
      the test path.
- [ ] `npx tsc --noEmit` clean.
